<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2002/33/eng@/~chp_II__cl_11__para_c> <https://schema.org/text> "by inserting after subsection (5) the following subsection: \"(6) In the application of subsection (4) in relation to a person's gross income from his employment where the expense, to which subparagraph (l)(b)(ii) applies is payable for a period (in this subsection referred to as the \"overlapping period\") which overlaps the basis 6 Bill period or part of the basis period, the amount of the expense to be deducted from that gross income shall be determined in accordance with the following formula: AxC B where A is the number of days accommodation is provided in the basis period or part of the basis period that falls in the overlapping period; B is the total number of days in the overlapping period; and C is the amount of expenses to which subparagraph (l)(b)(ii) applies.\". Amendment of section 60c"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/2002/33/eng@> .
